.TH edualc 1  edualc edualc
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
edualc \- Native desktop window for coding agents: Claude Code, agy and opencode
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBedualc\fR [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-\-permission\-mode\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-resume\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIDIR\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
A native desktop window for coding agents: Claude Code, agy and opencode.
.PP
Its arguments work like claude\*(Aqs own: the folder to work in, the model, a session to continue, and a first prompt. It needs the program it runs on the PATH: claude (Claude Code) by default, agy or opencode with \-\-backend.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<PROGRAM>\fR [default: claude]
The program to work with: claude (Claude Code), agy (Google\*(Aqs Antigravity CLI), or opencode
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
claude
.IP \(bu 2
agy
.IP \(bu 2
opencode
.RE
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
The model: for claude an alias such as sonnet, or a full name; for agy a name that `agy models` lists; for opencode one it offers once it runs
.TP
\fB\-\-permission\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
The permission mode to start in
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
default: Asks before edits and commands
.IP \(bu 2
acceptEdits: Edits without asking
.IP \(bu 2
plan: Reads and plans, edits nothing
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A classifier approves safe actions
.IP \(bu 2
bypassPermissions: Never asks. For throwaway sandboxes
.RE
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-resume\fR \fI<SESSION>\fR
A session to continue, by its id
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIDIR\fR]
The folder to work in. Without one or `\-\-resume`, opens the start page
.TP
[\fIPROMPT\fR]
A first prompt
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The window was closed.
.TP
\fB1\fR
edualc couldn\*(Aqt start its daemon or its window.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command line was wrong.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBCLAUDE_BIN\fR
The Claude Code program to run; claude on the PATH if unset.
.TP
\fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR
Claude Code\*(Aqs configuration folder; ~/.claude if unset.
.TP
\fBRUST_LOG\fR
Which messages are logged to standard error, as a tracing\-subscriber filter; edualc=info if unset.
.TP
\fBLC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG\fR
The first of these that is set to a Chinese, Japanese or Korean locale decides how text in Han characters alone is set, until you choose in the settings.
.TP
\fBNIRI_SOCKET\fR
Under niri, the start and project pages can focus the window of a session running elsewhere.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
Where the files below are kept.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/edualc/config.toml\fR
The settings you might change by hand (~/.config if unset).
.TP
\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/edualc/\fR
The daemon\*(Aqs socket.
.TP
\fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/edualc/\fR
What edualc keeps for itself (state.json) and what each turn changed (changes/), and what earlier versions left: the sandbox\*(Aqs folders, agy\*(Aqs data folders (agy\-homes/) and copies of agy\*(Aqs and opencode\*(Aqs transcripts (agy/, opencode/), which edualc no longer reads (~/.local/state if unset).
.TP
\fB$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects/\fR
Claude Code\*(Aqs transcripts, read for the start page, project lists and to continue sessions.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Claude Code: https://code.claude.com/docs/
.br
edualc: https://github.com/felintusun/edualc
